#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:124 cb9fec61895b4bad8411b90ac14b5300
msgid "Lost TOTP / authentication device?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:127 280753a3d25142a38868a03444666f9c
msgid ""
"In case you’ve lost your TOTP authentication device, you have two options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:129 3f0ad1433dc247e2810f473f59ed312d
msgid ""
"The first option is backup codes. When generating the TOTP secret you must "
"have saved some recovery codes. Those can be used in place of the TOTP code, "
"but they’re discarded after use. So make sure you redo the multi-factor "
"authentications intructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:131 a7e08275e75641639a7785a4ec0d4b60
msgid ""
"The second option is recovery from a backup. It will work as long as you "
"included dom0 in said backup. After restoring the dom0 backup, open a "
"terminal in dom0 and the file should be located in ``/home/<USER>/home-"
"restore-<DATE>/dom0-home/<USER>/.google_authenticator``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:134 822cd0a4eeb7458eba706bce526c6cac
msgid "Login with a YubiKey / NitroKey3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:137 e353df8f13514d2dbef13e8e147c6528
msgid ""
"The YubiKey / NitroKey3 is a hardware authentication device manufactured by "
"Yubico / NitroKey to protect access to computers, networks, and online "
"services that supports one-time passwords (OTP), public-key cryptography, "
"and authentication, and the Universal 2nd Factor `(U2F) <https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_2nd_Factor>`__ and FIDO2 protocols developed by "
"the `FIDO Alliance <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FIDO_Alliance>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:139 d6d47338189243e4a9c4690bbc4370a6
msgid ""
"You can use a YubiKey / NitroKey3 to enhance the user authentication in "
"Qubes. The following instructions explain how to setup the YubiKey / "
"NitroKey3 as an *additional* way to login."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:141 c33d834269ac477497a1f9fbcc946157
msgid ""
"After setting it up, you can login by providing both - a password typed in "
"via keyboard *and* the YubiKey / NitroKey3 plugged in. Someone eavesdropping "
"your login attempt would not be able to login by only observing and "
"remembering your password. Stealing your YubiKey / NitroKey3 would not "
"suffice to login either. Only if an attacker has both, the password and the "
"Yubikey / NitroKey3, it would be possible to login (it is thus called `Multi-"
"factor authentication <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-"
"factor_authentication>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:143 40fd63d7a441494e8a6a50c9703edef1
msgid ""
"The following instructions keep your current login password untouched and "
"recommends to define a new, additional password that is used in combination "
"with the YubiKey / NitroKey3 only. This ensures that you a) do not "
"accidentally lock yourself out during setup and b) you do not need to fear "
"`shoulder surfing <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Shoulder_surfing_(computer_security)>`__ so much (i.e. by not using your "
"standard login password in public)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:146 1f4785bc5c4f4b49a08382ca22fd3ac9
msgid "Setup login with YubiKey / NitroKey3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:149 86ccd05ad56f4d69b015dc33a98b8b3a
